Here is the commit message:
ACCUMULO-3937 Allow configuration in killing a tserver due to
 HDFS failures

Here is the root cause:
The bug arises from the lack of configurable parameters to manage the number of tolerated failures when creating a write-ahead log (WAL) file in HDFS. Without these parameters, the TabletServer may exit unexpectedly after encountering a fixed number of WAL creation errors, leading to potential service disruptions during HDFS failures.

Here is the patch:

